Subject: [PATCH 32/32] v10 raccord r2 closure: scope of the allow-single root
 rule stated, vote labels and leaf selection without a split

Minor findings of the adversarial re-verification on finding H2 (declared output change under --allow-single).
Comments and handover only, no code line changes.
- cli/mhgp10_cluster.cpp, header: the root rule applies to the label file, not to the .vote labels
  (--label=vote), which give each point the label of the retained cluster that covers it, with no lambda
  threshold: they stay those of the head, and a point the rule sends to noise keeps there the label 0 of the root
  that covers it. Under --selection=leaf without any split the root is retained with the same rule, while
  scikit-learn 1.9.1 retains no cluster: intended divergence, written in head.hpp.
- PASSATION.md, row "Tete sure": the same two statements.
Evidence (vote files identical to the head, count of noise points, 24 trials against scikit-learn itself) goes to
the closure receipt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
